Section: 4.3. Discussion
Text: 4.3. Discussion The data annotated in OGTD proved to be facilitating in offensive language detection with a signiﬁcant success for Greek, taking into consideration its size and label distri- bution, with the best model (LSTM and GRU with Atten- tion) achieving a F1-macro of 0.89. Among the classi- cal machine learning approaches, the linear SVM model achieved the best results, 0.80, whereas the the Stochastic Gradient Descent (SGD) learning classiﬁer yielded the best recall score for the Offensive class, at 0.61. In terms of features used, TF/IDF matrices of word unigrams proved to work work well with multiple classical ML classiﬁers.

