Text: This is mostly due to the availability of language resources for English. To address this shortcoming, this paper presents the ﬁrst Greek annotated dataset for offensive language identiﬁcation: the Offensive Greek Tweet Dataset (OGTD). OGTD is a manually annotated dataset containing 4,779 posts from Twitter annotated as offensive and not offensive. Along with a detailed description of the dataset, we evaluate several computational models trained and tested on this data.

